# Proposed by a fixer (2026-10-15), from the first run of F58's checks on a hosted Mac; the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: whoever presses ⌘M asked to be rid of a window. A person's ⌘M is never undone.
# When a window has landed in the Dock its app names its next window, and only then reports the minimizing. A held view sends the keyboard back to the
# window that is shown as soon as another is named, and giving a window the keyboard raises it, which fetches it out of the Dock: it flew
# there and straight back, in front of an audience. Now the window is asked first, and says itself where it is.
# Reference: F58, criterion 4. Decided in collab/QUESTIONS.md (product owner, 2026-10-15, "three things found behind green runs").
#
# Someone shares the screen with one Keynote window framed and the view held. Notes and a second Keynote window are out of view.
open Keynote
open Notes
open Keynote
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 right
zoom 101
hold
expect fills 101
minimize 101
flush
# It stays in the Dock, the view is empty and held, and nobody else has come into view.
expect hidden 101
expect hidden 102
expect hidden 103
expect held view
zoom 102
expect fail
# A click in the Dock brings it back to the same view.
restore 101
flush
expect fills 101
expect hidden 102
expect hidden 103
release
float-all
